{"findings":[{"file":"pkg/plugins/log/fake.go","line":46,"severity":"low","category":"test_gap","title":"TestLogger.FromContext returns a fresh logger, so recorded logs are lost","body":"`FromContext` returns `NewTestLogger()`. `LoggerMiddleware.logRequest` now logs through `m.logger.FromContext(ctx).Info(...)`. With this fake, the \"Plugin Request Completed\" call lands on a throwaway instance. The original `TestLogger`'s `InfoLogs` therefore stays at zero calls, and any test that asserts on those logs will fail or silently stop checking anything. `FromContext` should return the receiver (or a logger that shares its state). No test for `LoggerMiddleware` or the new `ContextualLoggerMiddleware` is added in this PR."},{"file":"pkg/services/pluginsintegration/clientmiddleware/contextual_logger_middleware.go","line":39,"severity":"low","category":"test_gap","title":"New middleware has no tests and does not guard against nil requests","body":"`ContextualLoggerMiddleware` takes over the contextual-logger behaviour that used to live in the instrumentation middleware, but no test covers it. That includes the endpoint, pluginId, dsName, dsUID and uname attributes it puts on the context. It also dereferences `req.PluginContext` without a nil check, whereas `LoggerMiddleware` explicitly guards `req == nil`. A nil request now panics here, in the new middleware, instead of passing through."},{"file":"pkg/services/pluginsintegration/clientmiddleware/logger_middleware.go","line":58,"severity":"medium","category":"bug","title":"traceID and request attributes now depend on middleware ordering and context-provider behaviour","body":"`logRequest` used to add `pluginId`, `endpoint`, `uname`, `dsName`, `dsUID` and `traceID` explicitly. It now relies entirely on `m.logger.FromContext(ctx)` picking up attributes set by `ContextualLoggerMiddleware`, plus traceID from the context. If `FromContext` fails the type assertion to `*log.ConcreteLogger`, the wrapper falls back to `d.New()`. That 